Author: Jeffrey Yu <jeffreyy@stanford.edu>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 04:14:22 2026 -0700

    feat: compile any network from settings instead of per-network rules
    
    - codegen.mk needed a new rule for every network, and the Sphinx firmware
      kit had no way to emit and link firmware without building a simulator.
    - Compile with one rule driven by MODE, CHECKPOINT, QCONFIG and SPEC_LENGTH
      that records each folder's settings, give CI's variants their own rows,
      add --build-only to run_voyager.py and stop relinking the emitter on
      every call; make -n gives all 21 existing networks their old commands.

